Given human abilities for organized hate toward other humans only
slightly different from them, I don't think the difference bweteen
symbol-based and connectionist AI will matter.  I think the key is the
degree to which AIs or uploads are integrated and mixed up with the
ordinary human society.  If AIs/uploads are creatures everyone works
closely with, have as friends and neighbors, and which share the same
political and economic institutions, then there is much less danger of
war.  If AIs/uploads are banished into space, as Morevac suggests, I
see much more danger.   [See my discussion in the next Extropy issue.]

